                <pb facs="1145" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1065"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bowen to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen reports that the plan suggested in the Department’s cable had already
                    been suggested by him to the President of Venezuela, by whom it was very
                    gracefully accepted; that the Venezuelan consul will now issue clearance papers
                    to the <hi rendition="#italic">Viking</hi> and inspect the ship before and after
                    each trip, so as to see that she carries only provisions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
